    "scientificThresholdsChanged": false,
    "meshDimensionalityCriterionChanged": true,
    "rationale": "The v1 mesh gate froze geometricDirections at 3. OpenFOAM classifies a wedge mesh as 2 geometric (non-empty/wedge) directions (1 1 0) and 3 solution (non-empty) directions (1 1 1), so that condition is unsatisfiable for any wedge topology and was never a statement about mesh quality; it was copied from the solution-direction line. The retained v1 mesh was otherwise healthy: Mesh OK, positive volume, one region, and exactly the six required patches. V3 is a new prospective contract that declares the wedge classification correctly before any v3 execution. It does not weaken, reinterpret, resume, or rerun v1 or v2, and no v1 or v2 observation may be reused as a v3 outcome. Asserting 2 geometric and 3 solution directions together is strictly more discriminating than v1's unsatisfiable pair, so this is a correction toward a stronger satisfiable gate rather than a relaxation. The reviewed product decision selecting this route is recorded in reviewDecision."
